Additional Use Grant: You may make production use of the Licensed Work, free of
                      charge, if Your use is Individual Use, Educational and
                      Research Use, Non-Profit Use, Public-Sector Use, Small
                      Organization Use or Small Product Use, each as defined
                      below. Any other production use requires a commercial
                      license from the Licensor.

                      "Individual Use" means use by a natural person who works
                      alone and on his or her own account, in any legal form,
                      including as a freelancer, consultant or sole proprietor,
                      or through a company in which that person is the only
                      person who works. A person works alone if no employee, no
                      partner who works in the business and no regular
                      contractor works for the business; contractors engaged
                      for a specific project are not counted. Individual Use is
                      free at any revenue. Individual Use does not include use
                      for the internal operations of an employer or of a
                      client: an employee who uses the Licensed Work for the
                      employer's work is making the employer's use, and the
                      category of the employer decides whether that use is
                      free. Running the Licensed Work as a continuing service
                      or pipeline for the internal operations of another
                      organization is that organization's use, on whatever
                      systems it runs, unless it is part of a product or
                      service of Your own described under Small Product Use.
                      Using the Licensed Work to prepare documents or other
                      deliverables for clients, one job at a time, is
                      Individual Use. Individual Use never includes a Competing
                      Offering.

                      "Educational and Research Use" means use by an accredited
                      school, college or university, or by its students and
                      staff, for teaching, learning or non-commercial academic
                      research.

                      "Non-Profit Use" means use by a Qualifying Non-Profit in
                      furtherance of its exempt purposes, and not in connection
                      with the sale of products or services (other than fees
                      that only recover the cost of its charitable activities).
                      A "Qualifying Non-Profit" is an organization that is
                      organized and operated exclusively for charitable,
                      educational, religious, scientific or similar
                      public-benefit purposes, whose net earnings do not
                      benefit any private person, and that is recognized as a
                      charity or as exempt from income tax on that basis under
                      the law of its jurisdiction (for example, under Section
                      501(c)(3) of the U.S. Internal Revenue Code, or as a
                      charity registered in the United Kingdom).

                      "Public-Sector Use" means use by a government department,
                      agency, municipality or other public authority for its
                      governmental functions. It does not include use by a
                      state-owned or government-controlled enterprise, or by
                      any body that sells products or services on a commercial
                      basis. Fees charged only to recover the cost of statutory
                      services are not a commercial basis.

                      Any organization that is not described in Individual Use,
                      Educational and Research Use, Non-Profit Use or
                      Public-Sector Use, including a company, partnership or
                      other business (with or without employees) and any
                      state-owned or government-controlled enterprise, is a
                      "For-Profit Organization". Production use by or for a
                      For-Profit Organization requires a commercial license
                      unless it is Small Organization Use or Small Product Use.

                      "Internal Use" means use of any part of the Licensed
                      Work, including the MCP server, the command-line tool,
                      the engine used as a library or imported into code, and
                      the validator, by an organization's own people, systems
                      and agents for its own operations. It includes scripts,
                      automation, continuous integration and delivery jobs,
                      batch jobs, internal pipelines, internal tools, AI agents
                      that run for the organization, and writing code against
                      the Licensed Work for those purposes. A license or grant
                      for Internal Use covers every part of the Licensed Work
                      together, on any number of computers, servers, agents and
                      pipelines; use is not counted per machine, server or
                      installation. Use for an organization's customers, or use
                      that lets third parties reach the Licensed Work, is not
                      Internal Use: it is Small Product Use or a Competing
                      Offering.

                      "Small Organization Use" means Internal Use by a
                      For-Profit Organization that, counting its affiliates
                      together with it, had both (a) total gross revenue below
                      USD 250,000 in its last completed fiscal year and (b) no
                      more than 10 people working for it at the end of that
                      fiscal year, or that has not yet completed a fiscal year
                      and reasonably expects to meet both limits in its first
                      one. The people working for it are its employees, its
                      owners and partners who work in it, and the individuals
                      who work for it on a regular basis as contractors,
                      counted as individuals and not as companies. Contractors
                      engaged for a specific project, servers, bots and AI
                      agents are not counted. Revenue in another currency is
                      converted into US dollars at the exchange rate on the
                      last day of the fiscal year. An "affiliate" is any entity
                      that controls, is controlled by, or is under common
                      control with another entity. "Control" means owning more
                      than 50% of the voting interests of an entity, or having
                      the power, by contract or otherwise, to direct its
                      management or policies. Customary minority-investor
                      rights, such as a board seat or consent rights over a
                      financing or a sale of the company, held with 50% or less
                      of the voting interests, are not control, and companies
                      that share only such an investor are not under common
                      control. Entities that are controlled by the same person,
                      or by persons acting together, are under common control.
                      An arrangement whose main purpose is to bring an
                      organization within a category above, or to keep it under
                      the limits of Small Organization Use or Small Product
                      Use, is disregarded.

                      "Small Product Use" means use of the Licensed Work as a
                      component of a product or service of Your own that has
                      substantial functionality beyond that of the Licensed
                      Work, if the revenue of that product or service in its
                      last completed fiscal year was below USD 250,000, or if
                      it has not yet completed a fiscal year and You reasonably
                      expect that to be so in its first one. The revenue of a
                      product or service is its gross revenue. Where it is sold
                      or provided as part of a bundle, suite or plan, the
                      revenue of every plan, module or edition that includes or
                      relies on the Licensed Work counts, and the revenue of
                      unrelated parts of a larger suite does not. A product or
                      service that You make available free of charge has no
                      revenue for this purpose, unless it is a free edition or
                      plan of a product that You also sell, in which case the
                      revenue of the paid editions counts. The size, the
                      headcount and the other revenue of Your organization do
                      not matter for Small Product Use. Your own Internal Use
                      of the Licensed Work is a separate matter: it is free
                      only under Individual Use or Small Organization Use, or
                      under a commercial license. Using the Licensed Work only
                      to develop and test the product is non-production use and
                      needs no category. Your customers and users may use the
                      Licensed Work only as part of that product or service. If
                      the Licensed Work is not delivered as part of Your
                      product, for example because users install it themselves,
                      each user's use of it is governed by that user's own
                      category. An arrangement whose main purpose is to keep
                      the revenue of a product under the limit, such as moving
                      revenue to another product, entity or period, is
                      disregarded.

                      No category above includes a Competing Offering, which
                      always requires a commercial license. A "Competing
                      Offering" is a product or service offered to third
                      parties whose value consists mainly of the functionality
                      of the Licensed Work. It includes hosting the Licensed
                      Work as a service for others; making the operations,
                      commands, API or tools of the Licensed Work available to
                      third parties as a service in itself, directly or through
                      a thin interface, for example through a public API or MCP
                      endpoint whose main purpose is access to the Licensed
                      Work; a desktop, web or other editor or application whose
                      value is mainly the document functionality of the
                      Licensed Work; and selling the Licensed Work, or a
                      product or service whose value is mainly the Licensed
                      Work, whether or not under another name. A product or
                      service is a Competing Offering if (a) most of what its
                      customers pay for, or use it for, is the document
                      functionality of the Licensed Work; (b) little of it
                      would remain without the Licensed Work, where an
                      interface, login, billing, prompts or similar layers
                      around the operations of the Licensed Work are not
                      features of its own; or (c) its main purpose is to let
                      third parties reach the operations, commands, API or
                      tools of the Licensed Work. A product or service that
                      uses the Licensed Work to implement substantial features
                      of its own is not a Competing Offering. This includes an
                      AI agent or an agent platform that uses the Licensed Work
                      as one of its tools: it is a product of Your own under
                      the paragraph above, and it needs a commercial license
                      once the limit of Small Product Use is reached.

                      You may copy, modify and redistribute the Licensed Work
                      free of charge, modified or not, provided that every copy
                      keeps this License and the copyright and license notices.

                      If You stop qualifying for a category above, You may
                      continue Your existing use for 90 days, and must then
                      obtain a commercial license or stop. For Small
                      Organization Use and Small Product Use, You stop
                      qualifying on the first day after the fiscal year in
                      which You passed a limit. This does not apply to an
                      organization that stopped qualifying because of an
                      arrangement that is disregarded above.

                      "Production use" means any use of the Licensed Work other
                      than non-production use, including making it part of a
                      product or service that You provide to others.
                      Non-production use (including evaluation, development,
                      testing and demonstration) is permitted by this License
                      without any category. Use is not non-production use
                      merely because it is called a pilot, test or staging use:
                      processing an organization's real documents as part of
                      its regular operations is production use, however the
                      environment is named. Documents and other output that You
                      create with the Licensed Work belong to You, and this
                      License places no restriction on them.

